# Project Overview

## Project Title
**Product Portfolio & Investment Analysis Using BCG Matrix**

## Project Background
Managing a diverse product portfolio requires businesses to understand product performance, market opportunities and competitive positioning. Analysing these factors helps management make informed decisions regarding resource allocation and investment priorities.

This project focuses on evaluating the product portfolio of a fictional FMCG company, Nova Consumer Products Ltd., using MySQL.

## Business Problem
The company needs to identify which products generate strong financial performance, which operate in growing or declining markets, and which products require additional investment or strategic review.

## Project Objectives
- Analyse product-wise sales and profitability.
- Evaluate year-on-year revenue and cost trends.
- Identify growing and declining product markets.
- Calculate relative market share to assess competitive strength.
- Classify products using the BCG Matrix.
- Develop product-level investment recommendations.

## Tools Used
- MySQL
- MySQL Workbench
- Microsoft Excel
- GitHub

## Project Scope
The analysis covers five datasets: Products, Sales, Market Data, Investments and Product Targets, covering the period 2021–2025.

## Expected Outcome
To transform structured business data into meaningful insights and develop strategic recommendations for product portfolio management and investment allocation.

**Note:** The project uses simulated data for educational and analytical purposes.

